    <Li>Definitions and interpretation
        <ol>
            <li>Definitions</li>
            <p>In these Terms:</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Account Customer</span> means a Customer whose Credit Application has been approved by the Company.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Business Day</span> means a day that is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday in Sydney.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Carriage</span> means the collection, transport, handling, storage in transit and delivery of Goods by any mode.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Carrier</span> means any person (other than the Company) that performs or arranges Carriage of the Goods, including road, rail, air and courier operators and their subcontractors, drivers and agents.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Carrier Terms</span> means the terms and conditions of carriage of the relevant Carrier, as amended from time to time, including any terms on its consignment note, website or rate schedule.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Convention</span> means any international convention, or law giving effect to one, that applies to international Carriage, including the Warsaw Convention (as amended) and the Montreal Convention 1999 as given effect by the Civil Aviation (Carrier’s Liability) Act 1959 (Cth).</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Company</span> means Freightonline Australia Pty Ltd ACN 131 492 576 trading as Couriers &amp; Freight.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Carrier Pallet Policy</span> means the pallet policy of the relevant Carrier, as amended from time to time.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Consequential Loss</span> means any loss of revenue, profit, opportunity, market, goodwill or reputation, loss from business interruption, and any loss that does not arise naturally in the usual course of things.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Consignment</span> means the Goods booked under a single consignment note or booking reference.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Credit Application</span> means the Company’s credit or account application signed by the Customer.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Customer</span> means the person who books, or on whose behalf is booked, the Services, and includes any person who signs a Credit Application or accepts these Terms online.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Dangerous Goods</span> means goods classified as dangerous goods under the Australian Dangerous Goods Code, the IATA Dangerous Goods Regulations or any Law, and any goods that are or may become hazardous, flammable, explosive, corrosive, toxic, radioactive or otherwise capable of causing harm to persons or property.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">FF Terms</span> means the Company’s Freight Forwarding Terms and Conditions, which apply to international freight forwarding, customs, import and export services.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Fees</span> means the Company’s charges for the Services as quoted, displayed at booking, set out in a rate schedule or the Credit Application or otherwise notified, together with all other amounts payable under these Terms.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Force Majeure Event</span> means any event beyond the reasonable control of the Company or a Carrier, including natural disaster, fire, flood, storm, epidemic, pandemic, road or rail closure, industrial action, civil unrest, acts of Government Authorities and failure of Carriers or suppliers.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">International Courier Services</span> means international express parcel, document and small freight services performed by international courier Carriers (such as DHL, FedEx, UPS, TNT and Aramex) under their own air waybills or consignment notes, where the Carrier (not the Company) arranges export and import customs clearance.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Goods</span> means the goods the subject of the Services, including their packaging, pallets and containers.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Government Authority</span> means any government or government agency, department, authority or body.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Law</span> means any law, regulation, code or binding direction of a Government Authority, including the Heavy Vehicle National Law.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Loss</span> means any loss, damage, cost, expense, fine, penalty, claim or liability, including legal costs on a full indemnity basis.</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Recharge</span> means any additional charge levied on the Company by a Carrier or other third party in respect of a Consignment after it was quoted, booked or invoiced, including adjustments for weight, dimensions or cubic volume, futile pick-ups, redelivery, redirection, waiting time, tail-lift, hand-unload, manual handling, residential delivery and other surcharges.</p>
            <p>Related Body Corporate has the meaning given in the Corporations Act 2001 (Cth).</p>
            <p><span class="bold">Pallets</span> means CHEP, LOSCAM or other branded hire pallets, and plain (unbranded) pallets.</p>
