    <li>Application of these Terms
        <ol>
            <li>These Terms apply to all domestic freight services and International Courier Services supplied by the Company, whether booked online, through an integration, by email, by phone or through an account.</li>
            <li>International freight forwarding services (including sea freight, air freight consolidation and customs brokerage arranged through freight forwarders) are governed by the FF Terms, not these Terms. If it is unclear which terms apply to a shipment, the Company will confirm this when quoting. Warehousing and 3PL services are provided by a separate business on its own terms and conditions, and are not governed by these Terms.</li>
            <li>The Customer accepts these Terms by signing a Credit Application, by accepting them when registering or booking online, or by instructing the Company to provide Services.</li>
            <li>If there is any inconsistency, the following order of priority applies: (a) a separate written agreement signed by both parties; (b) the Credit Application; (c) these Terms; and (d) any quotation. Clauses 3.4 to 3.7 apply despite this order of priority.</li>
            <li>Any terms and conditions of the Customer, including those on purchase orders or on the Customer’s own consignment notes, are excluded.</li>
            <li>The Company is not a common carrier and accepts no liability as a common carrier. The Company may refuse any booking or Goods without giving reasons.</li>
            <li>The Company may amend these Terms by giving at least 30 days’ written notice (including by email, or by publishing the amended Terms on its website and notifying Account Customers). Amended Terms apply only to Services booked after the date they take effect.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>The Company is a freight broker
        <ol>
            <li>The Customer acknowledges that the Company is a freight broker. The Company does not itself transport Goods. It arranges for Carriers to perform the Carriage.</li>
            <li>In arranging Carriage, the Company may contract with Carriers in its own name or as agent for the Customer, on the Carrier Terms, including terms that limit or exclude the Carrier’s liability.</li>
            <li>The Company may choose, add or change the Carrier, service level, route and method of Carriage for any Consignment, unless it has agreed in writing to use a particular Carrier or service.</li>
            <li>Carrier Terms bind the Customer. The Customer agrees that the Carriage of its Goods is subject to the Carrier Terms. The Customer is bound by, and must comply with, the Carrier Terms as if it were the customer or consignor named in them, including their exclusions and limitations of liability, time limits for claims, packaging and dangerous goods requirements, indemnities, liens and charges.</li>
            <li>Back-to-back obligations. The Customer’s obligations and liabilities to the Company in respect of a Consignment are no less than the Company’s obligations and liabilities to the Carrier in respect of the same Consignment. The Company’s liability to the Customer is no greater than the Carrier’s liability to the Company.</li>
            <li>Liability limited to amount recovered. For any loss of, damage to or delay in delivery of Goods, or other Loss, arising while the Goods are in the custody or control of a Carrier, or from any act or omission of a Carrier, the Company’s liability to the Customer is limited to the amount the Company actually recovers from the Carrier (or its insurers) in respect of that Loss, less the Company’s reasonable costs of recovery.</li>
            <li>On the Customer’s written request, the Company will lodge and pursue a claim against the Carrier on the Customer’s behalf, or assign to the Customer the Company’s rights against the Carrier, and will pay the Customer any amount recovered less its reasonable costs. The Customer must provide all information and evidence reasonably required to support the claim.</li>
            <li>Copies of the Carrier Terms for the Carriers the Company uses are available on request and, where practicable, are published on the Company’s website.</li>
            <li>Goods may from time to time be received, held, cross-docked or loaded at a depot operated by the Company or a Related Body Corporate. Any such Goods are held on behalf of, and as agent or subcontractor of, the relevant Carrier as part of the Carriage. The Company does not become the Carrier of the Goods, and clauses 3.4 to 3.7 and 4.2 continue to apply. To the extent the Company is nonetheless found to have any liability for Goods while at such a depot, that liability is limited under clause 12.4.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>Subcontractors and protection of third parties
        <ol>
            <li>Carriers and other subcontractors may further subcontract all or any part of the Services.</li>
            <li>Every exclusion, limitation, defence, immunity and indemnity in these Terms that benefits the Company also benefits each Carrier, subcontractor and Related Body Corporate of the Company, and each of their employees, drivers and agents. For this purpose the Company contracts as agent and trustee for each of them.</li>
