    </li>

    <li>Bookings, quotes and prices
        <ol>
            <li>Quotes and prices displayed on the Company’s website or booking platform are based on the information entered by the Customer (including weight, dimensions, number of items, pick-up and delivery locations, and whether they are business or residential addresses). They are estimates only until the Consignment has been collected and measured by the Carrier.</li>
            <li>Fees are calculated on chargeable weight, being the greater of the actual weight and the cubic weight using the conversion factor applied by the relevant Carrier for the service selected. Conversion factors are available on request.</li>
            <li>If the Carrier or the Company finds that any information provided by the Customer is incorrect (including weight, dimensions, item count, address type, or the Goods not being ready for collection), the Customer must pay the resulting adjustment and any Recharge, together with the recharge fee under clause 6.1.</li>
            <li>Fees are exclusive of GST unless stated otherwise, except that prices displayed to a Customer who is not registered for GST or is booking as a consumer will be shown inclusive of GST.</li>
            <li>Fees include the fuel levy and surcharges applicable at the time of booking. The Company may change its Fees at any time for future bookings. Changes to Fees agreed with an Account Customer in writing will be notified at least 30 days in advance, except for changes in Carrier fuel levies and surcharges, which may be passed on when they take effect.</li>
            <li>Any discount or rebate applies only if agreed by the Company in writing.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>Fees and charges
        <ol>
            <li>Recharges. The Customer is liable for all charges relating to its Consignments, including all Recharges. The Company may add a recharge fee of 3% (plus GST) of the amount of each Recharge.</li>
            <li>The following additional charges apply where relevant:
                <ol class="alpha" type="a">
                    <li>futile pick-up charges where the Goods are not ready, not accessible or not as described at the booked time, as charged by the Carrier;</li>
                    <li>redelivery, redirection, return and storage charges where Goods cannot be delivered for a reason not caused by the Carrier, as charged by the Carrier;</li>
                    <li>a manual consignment note fee where the Customer does not use the Company’s consignment note or labels, of $[●] per Consignment;</li>
                    <li>a fee of $150.00 (plus GST) per Consignment, plus all Carrier fines and charges, for undeclared or incorrectly declared Dangerous Goods; and</li>
                    <li>a dishonoured payment fee of $[●] (plus GST), plus any bank charges, for any payment that is dishonoured or reversed.</li>
                </ol>
            </li>
            <li>Account Customers must also pay any technology and services fees set out in Part B of their Credit Application.</li>
            <li>The Company does not charge a surcharge for payment by card.</li>
            <li>Where GST is payable on any supply under these Terms, the Customer must pay an additional amount equal to the GST at the same time as the Fees, subject to receiving a tax invoice.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>Payment
        <ol>
            <li>Customers without an approved account must pay at the time of booking. The Customer authorises the Company to charge the card or account used for the booking for any later adjustments, Recharges and fees relating to that booking.</li>
            <li>Account Customers must pay each invoice within 7 days of the invoice date, unless otherwise agreed in writing.</li>
            <li>The Customer remains liable for all Fees even if the Company agreed to invoice or collect them from a receiver or other third party and that person does not pay. Fees are payable whether or not the Goods are delivered, damaged or lost.</li>
            <li>The Customer must pay all amounts in full without set-off, counterclaim or deduction.</li>
            <li>If the Customer does not pay any amount by its due date:
                <ol class="alpha" type="a">
                    <li>interest is payable on the overdue amount at 2% per month (24% per annum), calculated daily from the due date until paid in full;</li>
                    <li>a late payment administration fee of $50.00 (plus GST) is payable for each invoice that remains unpaid 7 days after its due date, and a further $50.00 (plus GST) if it remains unpaid 30 days after its due date, reflecting the Company’s costs of following up overdue accounts; and</li>
                    <li>the Customer must pay all costs the Company incurs in recovering the overdue amount, including mercantile agent commissions and legal costs on a full indemnity basis.</li>
                </ol>
            </li>
            <li>If the Customer does not pay by the due date, or the Company reasonably believes the Customer may not be able to pay its debts, the Company may suspend or withdraw credit, require payment in advance, suspend the Services, exercise its lien under clause 15, and report the default to credit reporting bodies.</li>
            <li>If the Customer disputes an invoice, it must notify the Company in writing within 14 days of the invoice date, giving reasons, and must pay the undisputed portion by the due date.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

