    <li>Dangerous and prohibited goods
        <ol>
            <li>Unless the Company has agreed in writing in advance, the Customer must not tender: Dangerous Goods; cash, bullion, negotiable instruments, jewellery, precious metals or stones, artwork or antiques; perishable or temperature-sensitive goods; live animals or plants; firearms, weapons or ammunition; illegal goods; or any goods excluded by the Carrier Terms.</li>
            <li>If such goods are tendered, the Company and the Carrier may refuse, hold, return, destroy or otherwise deal with them at the Customer’s risk and expense, without liability. The Customer is liable for all Loss arising from them, and the Company has no liability for their loss or damage.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>Collection, delivery and pallets
        <ol>
            <li>Pick-up and delivery dates and times are estimates only and are not guaranteed.</li>
            <li>Delivery is complete when the Goods are delivered to the delivery address given by the Customer and a person at that address signs for them, or, where the Customer or receiver has given authority to leave, the Goods are left at that address. A Carrier’s proof of delivery (including an electronic signature or photograph) is evidence of delivery.</li>
            <li>If the Goods cannot be delivered for any reason not caused by the Carrier (including an incorrect or incomplete address, the receiver being unavailable or refusing delivery, or lack of access), the Company or the Carrier may store, redeliver, return or otherwise deal with the Goods at the Customer’s risk and expense.</li>
            <li>Pallets. The Company does not hold an account with CHEP, LOSCAM or any other pallet provider, and does not offer Pallet transfer, exchange or de-hire services. All Pallet movements, transfers, exchanges and control are the responsibility of the sender and the receiver.</li>
            <li>The Customer must comply with the Carrier Pallet Policy of the Carrier it books. In particular, the Customer must:
                <ol class="alpha" type="a">
                    <li>have any Pallet transfer arrangement it makes directly with a Carrier approved in writing by the Carrier before the first shipment;</li>
                    <li>record the number and type of Pallets on the Carrier’s consignment note or manifest, and complete a Pallet transfer docket signed by the Carrier’s driver (including the driver’s name and ID), failing which the Carrier may reject the transfer;</li>
                    <li>use plain Pallets for deliveries to receivers that do not hold an active pallet account, and to destinations where Pallets are unlikely to be recovered (such as mine sites, showgrounds and events); and</li>
                    <li>accept that branded Pallets sent to such receivers or destinations may be treated as the Customer’s own and not recovered, and that Carriers may adjust Pallet quantities where Pallets are unrecoverable.</li>
                </ol>
            </li>
            <li>Any Carrier charges relating to Pallets, including exchange, transfer, hire, loss or administration charges, are Recharges and are payable by the Customer together with the recharge fee under clause 6.1.</li>
            <li>The Company is not liable for any Loss relating to Pallets, including lost, stolen, missing, unrecoverable or unreturned Pallets, rejected or delayed transfers, or pallet hire charges. The Customer indemnifies the Company against any such Loss and any claim by a pallet provider, Carrier or receiver relating to Pallets.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>Warranty and insurance
        <ol>
            <li>No cover unless Warranty is purchased. The Company does not insure the Goods, and Goods are not covered by the Company for loss or damage unless the Customer selects and pays for the Warranty when booking, and the Warranty is shown in the booking confirmation.</li>
