            <li>If the Warranty has been purchased, it is provided on the WTCs, which form part of the contract for that Consignment and prevail over these Terms to the extent of any inconsistency in relation to Warranty claims.</li>
            <li>The Warranty is not insurance. The Customer is responsible for insuring its Goods for their full value while in transit and storage.</li>
            <li>If a Carrier offers its own transit warranty or insurance cover, that cover is provided on the terms of the Carrier or its insurer, and any claim is made against them.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>Liability
        <ol>
            <li>This clause 12 is subject to clause 19 and to any Law that cannot be excluded.</li>
            <li>The Goods are at the Customer’s risk at all times.</li>
            <li>Clause 3.6 applies to Loss arising while Goods are with a Carrier or from the acts or omissions of a Carrier. The Company is not otherwise liable for the acts or omissions of Carriers, provided it exercised reasonable care in selecting them.</li>
            <li>Except where the Warranty has been purchased (in which case the WTCs apply), where the Company is liable for loss of or damage to Goods (including under clause 3.9) and that liability is not otherwise excluded or limited by these Terms, its liability is limited to the least of:
                <ol class="alpha" type="a">
                    <li>the Customer’s actual loss;</li>
                    <li>the replacement cost of the Goods at the place and time they were collected; and</li>
                    <li>AUD $100 per Consignment, or such higher amount as applies under clause 19.3.</li>
                </ol>
            </li>
            <li>The Company is not liable for delay, or for failure to collect or deliver by any particular date or time.</li>
            <li>The Company is not liable for any Consequential Loss, however caused.</li>
            <li>The Company is not liable for any Loss arising from: information or instructions provided by or for the Customer; insufficient or improper packing, marking or labelling; inherent vice or the nature of the Goods; Goods tendered in breach of clause 8 or 9; the actions of any Government Authority; a Force Majeure Event; or a failure by a Carrier to collect cash on delivery (COD) payments.</li>
            <li>The limitations and exclusions in clauses 3.6 and 12.4 to 12.7 do not apply to Loss caused by the Company’s fraud or wilful misconduct.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

    <li>Claims and time limits
        <ol>
            <li>Any claim for damage to or partial loss of Goods must be notified to the Company in writing, with photographs, within 24 hours after delivery, so that the Company can lodge the claim with the Carrier within the Carrier’s time limits.</li>
            <li>Any claim for non-delivery of Goods must be notified to the Company in writing within 14 days after the date on which the Goods should have been delivered.</li>
            <li>The Company is discharged from all liability in connection with the Goods and the Services unless legal proceedings are commenced and written notice of them given to the Company within 9 months after the date the Goods were, or should have been, delivered.</li>
            <li>Where the Carrier Terms impose a shorter time limit, the Customer must comply with it, and the Company is not required to extend it.</li>
            <li>A failure to comply with the time limits in clauses 13.1 to 13.3 does not bar a claim to the extent the Company has not been prejudiced by the delay, including in its ability to claim against the Carrier or an insurer.</li>
            <li>The Customer must keep damaged Goods and their packaging available for inspection by the Company, the Carrier and their insurers, and must not dispose of them without the Company’s consent.</li>
            <li>The Customer must pay all Fees in full regardless of any claim, and must not deduct the amount of any claim from any payment.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

