    <li>Lien
        <ol>
            <li>The Company has a particular and general lien over all Goods and documents in its actual or constructive possession (including Goods held by a Carrier on its behalf) for all amounts owing by the Customer to the Company on any account, including the costs of exercising the lien.</li>
            <li>If any amount secured by the lien is not paid within 14 days after the Company gives the Customer written notice of its intention to sell, the Company may, subject to any applicable uncollected goods Law, sell the Goods by public auction or private sale, deduct all amounts owing and costs of sale from the proceeds, and pay any surplus to the Customer. Any shortfall remains payable by the Customer. Shorter or no notice may be given where the Goods are perishable or the cost of storing them is likely to exceed their value.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

