        <ol>
            <li>Terms used in this clause that are defined in the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 (Cth) (PPSA) have the same meaning as in the PPSA.</li>
            <li>The Customer grants the Company a security interest in all Goods (and their proceeds) that come into the possession or control of the Company or a Carrier on its behalf, to secure payment of all amounts owing by the Customer to the Company. The Customer consents to the Company registering and perfecting that security interest, and must do anything the Company reasonably requests for that purpose.</li>
            <li>To the extent permitted by the PPSA, the parties agree that sections 95, 118, 121(4), 130, 132(3)(d), 132(4), 135, 142 and 143 of the PPSA do not apply, and the Customer waives its right to receive a verification statement.</li>
            <li>This clause does not apply to Goods used predominantly for personal, domestic or household purposes.</li>
        </ol>
    </li>

